<title>POLAND: Polish construction rises 22.7 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Polish construction rises 22.7 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction output rose 22.7 percent in March and was 33.9 percent higher than in March 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p> POLISH CONSTRUCTION		MARCH     FEBRUARY   MARCH 1996</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)	  22.7	14.4 (14.0)   16.7</p>
<p> yr/yr change (pct)		  33.9	28.0	   -13.0</p>
<p> index (mthly avge 1994=100)     28.0     -10.3	   -18.1</p>
<p>					    JAN-MARCH 97    JAN-MARCH 96</p>
<p> pct change vs same period pvs yr     7.8		     8.2</p>
<p>NOTES - Revised data in brackets. March 1997 had 23 working days, February 1997 and March 1996 had 21 days.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
